 "applies_to": "Schneider Electric APC InRow RC ACRC301 chilled-water in-row coolers on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
 "summary": "Gateway profile for the APC ACRC301: 140 objects (117 AI, 23 AO), all polled. Outputs set cooling and supply air setpoints, airflow control, fan speed limits, delta-T setpoint, thresholds and startup/idle options; inputs give overall and group status, cool output and demand, rack, supply and return air temperatures, airflow, fan speed, chilled water valve, flow and temperatures, run hours and each alarm flag.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Schneider_Electric_ACRC301_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the ACRC301 Modbus register map (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/SchneiderACRC301.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "All 140 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (OUTPUT STATE 1); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
 ],
